---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Showing Sheep">
  <div class="bg-sage-800 text-white py-20 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-sage-300 text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Competitions</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl mb-6">Showing Sheep</h1>
      <p class="text-cream-200 text-xl max-w-2xl">Guidance on preparing and showing Portland sheep at breed and premier shows.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 prose prose-slate prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-sage-800">
    <h2>Premier Shows</h2>
    <p>The Group runs three Premier Shows each year — Midland, Northern and Southern. These are the flagship breed competitions, attracting entries from across the UK.</p>
    <h2>Judging Criteria</h2>
    <p>Portland sheep are judged on conformation, breed character, fleece quality and overall presentation. The breed standard emphasises the characteristic tan face, correct horn set in rams, and a compact, muscular body.</p>
    <h2>Show Classes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Ram — shearling or over</li>
      <li>Ram lamb</li>
      <li>Ewe — shearling or over</li>
      <li>Ewe lamb</li>
      <li>Pair — any age/sex</li>
      <li>Group of three</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Showing Fleece</h2>
    <p>Fleece classes are also offered at Premier Shows. Entries must be clean, rolled correctly and presented in accordance with the Group's fleece showing guidelines.</p>
    <p><a href="/contact/">Contact us</a> for the current show schedule and entry forms.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
